11. CaP-X environments, APIs, prompts and reference code
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------

Source: https://github.com/capgym/cap-x at commit 53e9966d7a8e2fa7494676772bccc35280f5c0ed
Where: runtimes/{capx,capx-libero}/robouse/src/robouse/backends/capx/capx_upstream/ (CaP-X's RoboSuite and LIBERO low-level environments, privileged APIs, PyRoKi IK snippets and controller configs, with its LICENSE and VENDORED.md); datasets/capx/*/task.md (CaP-X's task prompts and API documentation); datasets/capx/*/oracle/oracle_code.py (CaP-X's reference code)
Changes: listed in VENDORED.md (the PyRoKi server client replaced by the same solve in-process; unused perception imports removed; open3d imported only where used). The spill-wipe reference code wipes at z = -0.10 instead of 0.0 (stated in the file).
Dataset: capgym/cap-x (hub.yaml). The simulator images fetch at build time, and this repository does not contain: CaP-X's robosuite forks (https://github.com/uynitsuj/robosuite commit 97292732 and https://github.com/Max-Fu/robosuite commit a498b08, MIT, Copyright (c) 2022 Stanford Vision and Learning Lab and UT Robot Perception and Learning Lab), LIBERO-PRO with its scene assets (https://github.com/uynitsuj/LIBERO-PRO commit 5368540, MIT, Copyright (c) 2023 Lifelong Robot Learning) and PyRoKi (https://github.com/chungmin99/pyroki commit 95afccc, MIT).
